# Sync Devkit

Read the shared install receipt before version comparisons. An absent/invalid receipt means shared migration is pending even when an old compatibility version stamp equals the newest release. Inspect concrete selected provider bindings and installed mode/profile; mixed modes or nonterminal pipelines block without reset.

Resolve the GitHub devkit source owner/repository from the existing entrypoint, preserving its project content. Collect a bounded migration inventory with the shared engine; unknown older layouts receive inventory/conflicts only. Recognized v0.1.48-50 legacy content, including flat instructions and missing stamps, must be reviewed into explicit adaptations; custom conflicts are never solved by --auto. Preserve provider-local histories and strict counters.

Generate/review adaptive root/context/instruction content and exact hash-backed conflict resolutions. Print the complete plan before applying. Use the concrete Python 3.10+ interpreter and installed helper:

```text
python .mt-agent-devkit/scripts/sync.py --target . --repo <owner/repository> --provider <selected-provider> --mode <installed-mode> --profile <repo|project_root> --adaptations <reviewed-local-json> --output <provider-runtime-plan.json>
```

The helper resolves the release once, pins every read to the resulting commit, reads additive release-object deployment metadata, downloads/verifies every required asset before product writes and delegates to the shared transaction engine. It never fetches `/main` payloads. A missing deployment artifact stops safely; do not reinstall/reset a project or claim certification from an old stamp.

After authorized review, apply the same saved plan with `deployment.py apply --target . --plan <plan.json>`; avoid resolving the latest release again between plan and apply. Recovery uses the same journal/source identity with `deployment.py resume` or `rollback`. Successful receipt verification is the completion certificate. Report preserved content, exact written/retired paths, conflicts, pending recovery and native evidence limitations. No release is published by sync.
